<title>FRANCE: Aerospatiale to build second generation Meteosat.</title>
<headline>Aerospatiale to build second generation Meteosat.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Space Agency (ESA) said it had, in cooperation with the European Metrological Satellite Organisation, awared the contract for building three second-generation Meteosat satellites to Aerospatiale.</p>
<p>The contract amounts to more than 600 million ECUs.</p>
<p>The geostationary satellites will be launched from 2000 by Ariane and will give images at every 15 minutes instead of the current 30 miniutes.</p>
</text>
